From b0270d0bb30a1f017aa4d7c7233fd4bfe5701c82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:26:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] input: apple_n1: correct N1 timing and diagnose discovery
 failures

N1 configureSPI overrides provider setup offset 0x0c to zero. That field maps to WORD_DELAY, so retaining the ADT 5000 ns minimum was wrong. Keep the separate 10 us CS setup/hold timing.

Restore the additional 2 ms post-boot wait and per-GET delay. Wake on control attempts with the N1 100 ms suppression, and retry corrupt descriptor replies within one aggregate five-attempt budget. Preserve the verified wire packets and fail immediately on transport timeouts or malformed descriptors.

Trace bounded boot/control exchanges as well as runtime headers. Always identify echo/checksum, length/status, endian and surface failures and dump complete offending replies, without logging firmware or calibration payloads.
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_n1.c | 182 +++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 147 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

